  "_comment": "JS limits preserve bounded media failure reporting (#596): master measures 466.446 KiB on the route and 384.115 KiB in call scenarios. Compacting the classifier did not fit the old limits. Including media recovery (#594) and mic-state sync (#597) measures 468.243/385.808 KiB; 469/386 were the smallest whole-KiB limits above that combined build. The session ID (#670) adds its module, the Sync hello baggage and the legacy-Sync hello fallback, about 0.8 KiB gzip on the route; the combined build measures 469.5 KiB on the route in CI, which did not fit 469, so the route limit is 470, the smallest whole-KiB limit above it. TURN credentials (#676) add the SDK's ICE-server parsing and its use when a peer connection opens, which buys connecting on networks that block UDP. Five runs each on Instabox (AMD EPYC, 4 vCPU, Node 24.21.0, pnpm 12.8.1, Chromium 151.0.7922.34) measure 470.123 KiB on the route for the merge with master and 469.914 KiB for master, min, median and max identical because gzip bytes are deterministic; CI measured 470.1 (Gate run 41209697376). The added code costs 0.21 KiB, and the clean trims I tried saved 0.05 KiB of the 0.12 needed, so the route limit is 471, the smallest whole-KiB limit above 470.1. Per-call stats (#671) add the collector, the summary fields and the upload transport, about 1.8 KiB gzip on the route, which buys loss, RTT and bitrate summaries from real calls. Five production builds each on Instabox (AMD EPYC, 4 vCPU, Node 24.21.0, Chromium 151.0.7922.34) measure 470.6 KiB for master 919d1fda9 and 472.4 KiB for the merge with #671 (acb96ff10), min, median and max identical; the call-scenario build measures 378.9 KiB against its limit of 386. The call-performance lane is not selected on #671, so no CI number exists. The 471 limit does not fit 472.4, so the route limit is 473, the smallest whole-KiB limit above it. Including the camera background feature (#646) measures 473.470 KiB on this branch versus 472.364 KiB on current master cfa93d0f5, with five isolated route loads per production build on the same Linux Intel Xeon host (Node 24.19.0, pnpm 12.8.1, Chromium 151.0.7922.34), min, median and max identical. The 473 ceiling cannot contain both features; 474 is the smallest whole-KiB ceiling that fits. The pinned baseline commit predates the route measurement and stays as is. The call-scenario limit (386) and all other limits stay unchanged.",
